[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3394127072","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111546#issuecomment-3394127072","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111546","id":3394127072,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7KTkTg","user":{"login":"Mickeon","id":66727710,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NzI3NzEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/66727710?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Mickeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-12T10:14:08Z","updated_at":"2025-10-12T10:14:08Z","body":"> In addition to providing autocomplete for the animation name argument, autocomplete support for marker names is also added. This requires modifying `Object::get_argument_options()`'s signature and passing a list of resolved arguments, but as this virtual method isn't exposed to ClassDB to begin with, compatibility is not affected.\r\n\r\nWhile I was eventually considering this personally, I feel like the addition is quite intrusive in this PR. It affects **all** code implementing `get_argument_options`, regardless of whether they make use of it. Don't get me wrong, there's plenty of methods out there that could use previous arguments to predict new ones, but could there not be something less invasive for now?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3394127072/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3394129861","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111546#issuecomment-3394129861","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111546","id":3394129861,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7KTk_F","user":{"login":"chocola-mint","id":56677134,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2Njc3MTM0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56677134?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint","html_url":"https://github.com/chocola-mint","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-12T10:18:55Z","updated_at":"2025-10-12T10:18:55Z","body":"> While I was eventually considering this personally, I feel like the addition is quite intrusive in this PR. It affects **all** code implementing `get_argument_options`, regardless of whether they make use of it. Don't get me wrong, there's plenty of methods out there that could use previous arguments to predict new ones, but could there not be something less invasive for now?\r\n\r\nAnother option would be to add a second virtual method `get_argument_options_contextual()` that takes the additional argument, keep `get_argument_options()`'s signature as-is, and call both in `gdscript_editor.cpp`. Would that sound better?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3394129861/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3394139147","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111546#issuecomment-3394139147","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111546","id":3394139147,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7KTnQL","user":{"login":"Mickeon","id":66727710,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NzI3NzEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/66727710?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Mickeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-12T10:34:37Z","updated_at":"2025-10-12T10:34:37Z","body":"Maybe I'm just exaggerating, and an eventual addition to this method was necessary, regardless of the PR that did it. I'm not personally against the above suggestion, but perhaps anyone else can chime in on this.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3394139147/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3394367364","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111546#issuecomment-3394367364","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111546","id":3394367364,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7KUe-E","user":{"login":"HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction","html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-12T13:02:52Z","updated_at":"2025-10-12T13:02:52Z","body":"Methods which require argument context are currently implemented directly in the autocompletion code. You can look at `tween_property` for an example.\r\n\r\nThere are users asking to expose `get_argument_options`. I'd rather not add additional features to it, if we want to move forward with that. It will just make it harder to convert this to a user facing api.\r\n\r\nAs for adding another virtual method: The design of `get_argument_options` is inherently flawed in that it requires an instance of the object. This makes the cases were it actually can be used limited. I'd rather not add a new generalized system with the same flaw.\r\n\r\nI think in the future the `get_argument_option` system should be converted to some other API that works based on type information instead of instances. When we do that we can look into adding a generalized API for argument context.\r\n\r\nBut for now this should just be solved with a hardcoded special case in the autocompletion code IMO.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3394367364/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3394543923","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111546#issuecomment-3394543923","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111546","id":3394543923,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7KVKEz","user":{"login":"chocola-mint","id":56677134,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2Njc3MTM0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56677134?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint","html_url":"https://github.com/chocola-mint","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-12T14:26:16Z","updated_at":"2025-10-12T14:26:16Z","body":"> But for now this should just be solved with a hardcoded special case in the autocompletion code IMO.\r\n\r\nI've gone ahead and rewritten the PR according to this.\r\n\r\nIn addition, I've improved the marker autocomplete so it will only suggest markers that won't cause `play_section_with_markers()` to fail. (That is, if the start marker is filled, then the end marker suggestion will only contain markers that come *after* the start marker, and vice versa)\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c1d7e5f1-48f4-4590-8e8f-8ab565119915","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3394543923/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3564689041","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111546#issuecomment-3564689041","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111546","id":3564689041,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7UeNaR","user":{"login":"lyuma","id":39946030,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5OTQ2MDMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/39946030?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma","html_url":"https://github.com/lyuma","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-21T21:46:24Z","updated_at":"2025-11-21T21:46:24Z","body":"We're in favor of the change in the animation meeting. Should we add set_section_with_markers too? (Will be argument indices 0 and 1 in this case...)\r\n\r\nDidn't test it because I don't have animations with markers","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3564689041/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]